module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.instrument_blind_spot_anti_correlated_with_severity

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data instrument_blind_spot_anti_correlated_with_severity: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "instrument_blind_spot_anti_correlated_with_severity" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an instrument loses its subject precisely as that subject becomes severe enough to act on, so the evidence required to justify a repair is destroyed by the condition the repair would fix** (INVALID STATE: an instrument accumulates observations and publishes them at a completion boundary; a subject that exceeds a limit never reaches that boundary; so the observation is dropped, and the instrument reports the subject as ABSENT rather than as LOST. ",

    "The omission is not random -- it is a monotone function of severity, so the instrument is quietest about exactly the population it exists to surface. ",

    "MECHANISM, in the instance measured: the required floor's cross-claim demand census absorbs a claim's producer demands when the claim RETURNS. ",

    "A claim preempted by the per-claim deadline never returns. ",

    "So the producer whose cost CAUSED the preemption contributes no row, and a reader asking `which producers does this run re-derive across claims` is answered without it. ",

    "MEASURED on main run 34085084808: the census summary reports `claim_cpu_censored_rows_excluded=4`, and that run had exactly four interrupted claims -- the three `outside_modeled_guarantee_witness_test` rows and one determinism row. ",

    "No row is printed for `v2.std.decl_index.decl_facts`, for `v2.lens.module_graph.module_declaration_facts_live`, or for the nullary producer that reads them, which are the producers those three claims were preempted by. ",

    "The same summary declares `omitted_under_floor` counters bounding what no artifact retains, so the census is a lower bound with a declared blind spot even before this class applies. ",

    "HARM: an enrolment proposal evidenced from that census would have been evidenced from an artifact structurally unable to contain its subject, and the shape of the failure is the one DESIGN section 5 ranks worst -- not an error but a well-formed answer to the wrong population. ",

    "A reader cannot tell `this producer is not re-derived` from `this producer's demands were lost with a preempted claim`, and the two prescribe opposite actions: leave it alone, or enrol it. ",

    "THE CHEAP RECOGNITION RULE, and it costs one line of a summary: compare the censored-row count to the interrupted-claim count, then check whether the instrument prints a row for the producer those claims were preempted by. ",

    "Equal counts with no such row is this class. ",

    "WHY IT IS NOT A GATE DEFECT, which is why it sits unnoticed: the census gates nothing and enrols nothing by its own declaration -- its code says so in the same breath as naming the roster it feeds. ",

    "Nothing refuses, nothing is blocked, and no verdict is wrong today. ",

    "It is an EVIDENCE-AVAILABILITY defect: it silently bounds what anyone can ever prove about the population it drops, and a bound on provability produces no symptom until someone tries to prove the thing. ",

    "WHY IT IS NOT `absorbing_fallback`: that class substitutes a superset when a precise answer is unavailable, and its tell is a widening failure arm. ",

    "Here nothing widens and nothing is substituted -- the arm simply never runs, and the count of what it skipped is published honestly. ",

    "The defect is that the published count is never JOINED to the identities it skipped, so an honest aggregate stands in for a missing per-subject fact. ",

    "WHY IT IS NOT `salience_instrument_blind_to_the_record_it_sizes`, which is the nearest neighbour and also an instrument-blindness class: there the instrument reports a NUMBER that is wrong for one representation, and the harm is misallocated attention on a record everyone can see. ",

    "Here the record is not misreported, it is ABSENT, and its absence is indistinguishable from the subject never having occurred. ",

    "The two also differ in direction of dependence: diff size is wrong as a function of REPRESENTATION and is equally wrong for a trivial and a substantive edit, while this blindness is a function of SEVERITY and is zero until the subject crosses a limit. ",

    "That monotonicity is the whole class and is what makes it worth a row of its own. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1, mitigatable. ",

    "The censored count IS emitted, so a reader who thinks to compare it against the interrupted-claim count can detect the condition; safety depends entirely on that comparison occurring to someone. ",

    "CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed. ",

    "Which producers a preempted claim had demanded is known to the instrument at preemption time -- the demands are accumulated as evaluation proceeds and only the ABSORPTION is deferred to return -- so a typed censored-demand row naming the claim and the identities lost with it is derivable rather than requiring a new measurement. ",

    "It cannot reach 4: the claim really is preempted and its demand set really is partial, so `partial` is a state the model must be able to represent rather than one it can make unwritable. ",

    "NEXT TRIGGER, NAMED AS THE CAPABILITY: **the demand census emits, for every preempted claim, the producer identities whose demands were unabsorbed, as rows typed distinctly from ordinary demand rows** -- sufficient for a consumer reading the artifact alone to distinguish `not demanded` from `demanded and lost`, demonstrated by a discriminating red on a fixture run carrying one interrupted claim whose producer appears in neither population. ",

    "Raising the per-claim limit does NOT discharge this: it moves which claims are censored without making any censored claim's demands visible, and it changes the thing being measured, which is the remedy DESIGN section 5 would call a widen rather than a repair.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
